1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:00,840
Ouch!

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,700
That sound.

3
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:03,380
Ow!

4
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:05,520
Two spellings make it.

5
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,240
Ou, and ow.

6
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:09,760
Say it with me.

7
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:11,260
Ow!

8
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:13,930
You hear it in cloud.

9
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:16,120
And in cow.

10
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,840
Same sound, different spelling.

11
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,000
So which one do we write?

12
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,000
It's the same secret as always.

13
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,840
WHERE the sound sits in the word.

14
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,840
Ou likes the beginning and the middle.

15
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:31,060
Never the end.

16
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:32,060
Look.

17
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:33,480
Out.

18
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,980
Cl-ou-d.

19
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,840
H-ou-se.

20
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:42,880
Ou stays tucked inside the word.

21
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,620
Ow takes the END of the word.

22
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,180
C-ow.

23
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,600
N-ow.

24
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,820
H-ow.

25
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,060
Nothing comes after it.

26
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:57,060
And here's a bonus.

27
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:02,270
Ow also works right before a final n or l.

28
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,660
Br-ow-n.

29
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,400
T-ow-n.

30
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:08,960
Ow-l.

31
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,080
Now, one important thing about ow.

32
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,480
Do you remember our oa and ow video?

33
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:19,560
In that one, ow was saying the long O.

34
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,040
Snow.

35
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:22,380
Grow.

36
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:23,820
Show.

37
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:28,080
But here, ow is saying ow!

38
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:29,720
Cow.

39
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:31,240
Brown.

40
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:32,560
Owl.

41
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:34,980
Same two letters.

42
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,880
Two completely different sounds!

43
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:39,820
So how do you know which sound to say?

44
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,040
Here's the honest answer.

45
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,200
The letters don't tell you.

46
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:46,520
There is no rule for this one.

47
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,540
You have to test it.

48
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,120
Watch me.

49
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,060
Sn-ow.

50
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,550
With the long O, that gives me snow.

51
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:57,320
Snow is a real word!

52
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,720
So that one is right.

53
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:00,220
Now this one.

54
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,800
C-ow.

55
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:06,390
With the long O, that gives me coe.

56
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,780
Coe is not a word.

57
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,500
So I switch to the other sound.

58
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:11,720
C-ow.

59
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,500
Cow!

60
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:15,660
There it is.

61
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,100
That's the trick.

62
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:19,980
Try one sound, then try the other.

63
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,600
Keep the one that makes a real word.

64
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,530
And don't worry.

65
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:26,850
Our spelling rule still works perfectly.

66
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:32,060
When you WRITE, ou goes inside, and ow goes at the end.

67
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:34,720
It is only the SOUND you have to test.

68
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:36,480
Let's see them.

69
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:37,620
Out.

70
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:39,280
Cloud.

71
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:40,700
House.

72
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,020
Mouth.

73
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:43,700
Round.

74
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,180
Shout.

75
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,350
Every one has ou inside.

76
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:50,040
Now the ow words.

77
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:51,440
Cow.

78
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:52,980
Now.

79
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:54,500
How.

80
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,260
Wow.

81
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:57,840
Brown.

82
00:02:58,900 --> 00:02:59,420
Owl.

83
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,320
Ow at the end, or guarding that final letter.

84
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:04,920
Your turn!

85
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:06,930
Here's the word.

86
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,180
Brown.

87
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,910
Is it ou, or ow?

88
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:12,800
It's ow!

89
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:16,360
Because ow can sit right before a final n.

90
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,860
So remember.

91
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,640
Ou hides inside.

92
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,140
Ow finishes the word, or guards the last letter.

93
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,140
And ow always has two sounds to try.

94
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:29,540
Want to hear every sound like this?

95
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,160
The English Learning app is free.

96
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:33,420
Go and explore!
